    "title": "What channel is Duke women's basketball vs UCLA? Time, TV for game",
    "text": "Updated March 29, 2026, 12:20 p.m. ETNo. 3-seeded Duke women's basketball (27-8) survived and advanced from the Sweet 16 of the NCAA Women's Tournament, unleashing revenge on LSU, 87-85, on March 27.Up next for the Blue Devils to attempt to eliminate is 1-seed UCLA (34-1), which beat California Baptist 96-43 in the first round, Oklahoma State 87-68 in the second round and Minnesota 80-56 in the Sweet 16 to secure its spot here.Duke and UCLA played each other in November in Las Vegas. The Bruins walked away victorious from that one, 89-59 in Michelob ULTRA Arena for the Players Era Championship on Nov. 27.Looks like the revenge tour isn't over yet for the Blue Devils.Here's what to know about Duke-UCLA women's basketball in the Elite Eight of the NCAA Women's Tournament on Sunday as part of the Sacramento Regional 2:Buy Duke women's basketball ticketsWhat channel is Duke vs UCLA women's basketball on?TV channel: ABCStreaming: ESPN Unlimited, FuboDuke vs. UCLA women's basketball is being broadcast on ABC and will be available for streaming via ESPN Unlimited or Fubo, which offers a free trial for new subscribers.Duke vs UCLA women's basketball start timeDate: Sunday, March 29Time: 3 p.m. ETDuke vs. UCLA women's basketball tips off at 3 p.m. ET from Golden 1 Center in Sacramento, Calif., on Sunday, March 29.Duke vs UCLA women's basketball historySeries record: Tied, 2-2Duke's last win: Nov. 10, 2000; 80-52UCLA's last win: Nov. 27, 2025; 89-59Duke women's basketball schedule 2025-26Record: 27-8 overall, 16-2 ACCNovember (3-5)Nov. 3: Baylor 58, Duke 52Nov. 9: Duke 91, Holy Cross 48Nov. 12: Duke 83, Norfolk State 32Nov. 14: West Virginia 57, Duke 49Nov. 16: Duke 71, Liberty 57Nov. 20: South Florida 85, Duke 72Nov. 26: South Carolina 83, Duke 66Nov. 27: UCLA 89, Duke 59December (4-1)Dec. 4: LSU 93, Duke 77Dec. 7: Duke 70, Virginia Tech 54Dec. 18: Duke 97, South Dakota State 54Dec. 20: Duke 76, Belmont 46Dec. 28: Duke 71, Syracuse 51January (8-0)Jan. 1: Duke 100, Boston College 49Jan. 4: Duke 82, Notre Dame 68Jan. 8: Duke 78, Cal 74Jan. 11: Duke 67, Stanford 60Jan. 15: Duke 65, Virginia 58Jan. 18: Duke 93, Georgia Tech 46Jan. 24: Duke 95, Pitt 41Jan. 29: Duke 74, Miami 58February (6-1)Feb. 1: Duke 80, Wake Forest 44Feb. 5: Duke 59, Louisville 58Feb. 8: Duke 95, SMU 36Feb. 15: Duke 72, UNC 68Feb. 19: Duke 83, NC State 65Feb. 22: Clemson 53, Duke 51Feb. 26: Duke 80, Florida State 52March (6-1)March 1: UNC 74, Duke 69March 6: Duke 60, Clemson 46March 7: Duke 65, Notre Dame 63March 8: Duke 70, Louisville 65 (OT)March 20: Duke 81, Charleston 64March 22: Duke 69, Baylor 46March 27: Duke 87, LSU 85March 29: vs. UCLA, 3 p.m. ET (ESPN)AprilApril 3: NCAA Women's Final Four — Phoenix, Ariz.April 5: NCAA Women's Championship — Phoenix, Ariz.Our team of savvy editors independently handpicks all recommendations. If you purchase through our links, the USA TODAY Network may earn a commission. Prices were accurate at the time of publication but may change.",
